Pakistanis don't spend on their experience.

54
00:02:54,840 --> 00:03:00,280
One reason is that income disparity is high in both countries.

55
00:03:00,360 --> 00:03:04,040
No matter where they live, because the challenges are back home.

56
00:03:04,120 --> 00:03:07,120
Here you have to pay a bill of one lakh rupees for electricity.

57
00:03:07,200 --> 00:03:08,640
Delhi has to pay two hundred rupees.

58
00:03:08,720 --> 00:03:10,640
You get what I'm saying? There is a lot of expenditure here.

59
00:03:10,720 --> 00:03:13,120
So even if they live outside, they have to think about the back end.

60
00:03:13,200 --> 00:03:15,160
So, one thing is that they don't spend on their experience.

61
00:03:15,240 --> 00:03:18,880
Even if there are tickets, they give more to sell in black.

62
00:03:18,960 --> 00:03:22,080
We have seen it on TV all our lives, we will see it on TV this time too.

63
00:03:22,160 --> 00:03:24,320
So it's always 90 to 10.

64
00:03:24,400 --> 00:03:27,600
90% Indian crowd and 10% Pakistani crowd.

65
00:03:27,680 --> 00:03:30,640
It was the same in Melbourne, the T20 match.

66
00:03:30,720 --> 00:03:33,640
I don't even remember now, it was the World Cup.

67
00:03:33,720 --> 00:03:35,280
That was also the World Cup.

68
00:03:35,360 --> 00:03:39,200
And here too, literally 90 to 10 ratio was there.

69
00:03:39,280 --> 00:03:41,600
And Indian fans were totally quiet.

70
00:03:41,680 --> 00:03:43,030
They had lost hope.

71
00:03:43,110 --> 00:03:46,030
Because it was a match that was going on.

72
00:03:46,110 --> 00:03:51,030
In fact, after the first inning, when I went outside, they were drinking, they were like, we're not interested.

73
00:03:51,110 --> 00:03:56,030
It's a one-sided match. But then whatever happened, we all saw. Horrible, horrible experience.

74
00:03:56,110 --> 00:04:03,030
I met a lot of people who told me a lot of things. I wish I could share that on screen, but I can't. Controversies are made.

75
00:04:03,110 --> 00:04:07,030
There are legal implications as well. So, I shouldn't say.

76
00:04:07,110 --> 00:04:10,630
However, like a gentleman who himself packed the nihari.

77
00:04:10,710 --> 00:04:15,490
They were even abusing him for eating nihari yesterday and then they took the parcel.

78
00:04:15,570 --> 00:04:18,243
Now, if it's about professionalism, for example,

79
00:04:18,323 --> 00:04:21,189
if I have an appearance somewhere in the morning,

80
00:04:21,269 --> 00:04:26,721
or if I have a show or I have to go to a university or I have to go for a shoot in the morning,

81
00:04:26,801 --> 00:04:31,850
then I will try to sleep at 10.30 or 11.30 so that I get a full 8-hour sleep and I go fresh.

82
00:04:31,930 --> 00:04:35,730
Right? But here you are playing an international match.

83
00:04:36,890 --> 00:04:41,130
It's a match between Pakistan and India.

84
00:04:41,210 --> 00:04:42,130
Right?

85
00:04:42,210 --> 00:04:46,170
You're not just eating nihari, you're also parceling it.

86
00:04:46,250 --> 00:04:59,050
So obviously, when you're having nihari for dinner, you can't compete with Virat Kohli.

87
00:04:59,130 --> 00:05:00,050
Never.

88
00:05:00,130 --> 00:05:02,050
But there is no professionalism.

89
00:05:02,130 --> 00:05:03,760
I came across a lot of other things.

90
00:05:03,840 --> 00:05:09,360
things but I won't share that on screen. So then it's a very non-serious attitude but then it stems from the top.

91
00:05:09,440 --> 00:05:15,760
You can see on the top. Yesterday in Sawat, a man was burnt alive on alleged blasphemy allegations.

92
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:20,600
And the way it happens, we all have seen it. If someone has a fight, they are brought to the blasphemy case.

93
00:05:20,680 --> 00:05:26,760
Apparently that guy was with his family staying in Sawat from 18th June. Right?

94
00:05:26,840 --> 00:05:31,510
They went on a holiday. So many people are saying that there must have been a fight on Bilbil or something.

95
00:05:31,590 --> 00:05:33,510
or something else and put a charge on it.

96
00:05:33,590 --> 00:05:36,510
And it's very easy in Pakistan, as we've all seen.

97
00:05:36,590 --> 00:05:38,970
But after this incident, Mohsin Naqvi Sahib,

98
00:05:39,050 --> 00:05:42,267
who is the chairman of PCB and also the Interior Minister,

99
00:05:42,347 --> 00:05:44,510
he was eating kebabs on the same kebabs.

100
00:05:44,590 --> 00:05:47,590
Meaning, you know, the fish rots from the top.

101
00:05:48,160 --> 00:05:52,078
If there is such a big incident in your country and you are the Interior Minister,

102
00:05:52,158 --> 00:05:53,703
the last thing you would want is,

103
00:05:53,783 --> 00:05:56,544
if you go to eat kebabs and then the incident has happened,

104
00:05:56,624 --> 00:05:58,590
then at least you know that I don't tweet.

105
00:05:58,770 --> 00:06:02,370
It won't fly, it won't sit well with the people. But they tweeted.

106
00:06:02,450 --> 00:06:04,690
They don't have any tension.

107
00:06:04,770 --> 00:06:07,410
And so that is unprofessionalism.

108
00:06:07,490 --> 00:06:12,850
So when you see your elders with such a non-serious attitude, then you will see that in every department.

109
00:06:12,930 --> 00:06:15,570
You can see that in cricket too. They don't care, they don't give a damn.

110
00:06:15,650 --> 00:06:19,570
The tournament is over, it's time. I stayed for four more days.

111
00:06:19,650 --> 00:06:23,170
And then it took me three days to come here. I'll tell you the story.

112
00:06:23,250 --> 00:06:26,650
But our players are still in America because.

113
00:06:27,040 --> 00:06:33,680
So yeah, so this is the situation. Then the match in Canada was okay. I cancelled Florida anyway.

114
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:38,840
And I hadn't made a trip for West Indies from the start because I was hopeful that they wouldn't be able to go ahead.

115
00:06:38,920 --> 00:06:39,780
And I was right.

116
00:06:39,860 --> 00:06:41,070
So we cancelled Florida.

117
00:06:41,150 --> 00:06:46,040
I had nothing else to do because the guy had planned that he wanted to stay for 20 days.

118
00:06:46,120 --> 00:06:48,040
The world's eighth day ended here.

119
00:06:48,120 --> 00:06:53,540
So then I went to Atlantic City because it was close to New York. My friend wanted to take me there.

120
00:06:53,620 --> 00:06:59,900
We had a good time. It's like, you know, you can say, a broken Vegas.

121
00:06:59,980 --> 00:07:05,140
So we were there and then I was supposed to fly from Philadelphia.

122
00:07:05,220 --> 00:07:09,100
I didn't get a return ticket. Again, I didn't know when the World Cup was ending.

123
00:07:09,180 --> 00:07:11,740
So we flew from Philadelphia. Now you have to listen to this story.

124
00:07:11,820 --> 00:07:15,860
I was supposed to fly via Qatar to Karachi.

125
00:07:15,940 --> 00:07:20,460
As soon as the plane went into the air, a man got a serious attack.

126
00:07:20,890 --> 00:07:25,410
announced that any doctor on board, two or three people were standing, there was a nurse, there were two doctors.

127
00:07:25,490 --> 00:07:31,410
So they checked and they said, man, he won't be able to cross the Atlantic Ocean, he needs to go to the hospital.

128
00:07:31,490 --> 00:07:34,610
So we decided to, the pilot decided to land in Boston.

129
00:07:34,690 --> 00:07:39,610
So Boston was nearby, and when we landed there, the emergency personnel immediately took the person.

130
00:07:39,690 --> 00:07:41,210
Now the plane didn't move.

131
00:07:41,290 --> 00:07:47,410
Then the pilot said, yes, we landed very hard, so the tires are still warm, so let the tires cool down, then we will go.

132
00:07:47,490 --> 00:07:48,040
Now it took an hour.

133
00:07:48,120 --> 00:07:49,860
It took an hour for the tires to cool down.

134
00:07:49,940 --> 00:07:53,040
Then he said, there's no jet bridge available, so we're going to the other gate.

135
00:07:53,120 --> 00:07:54,280
And I was like, wait a minute.

136
00:07:54,360 --> 00:07:57,620
When the patient has left, why do we need a jet bridge?

137
00:07:57,700 --> 00:08:01,040
Jet bridge is the bridge that the passengers get off from.

138
00:08:01,120 --> 00:08:03,540
So I thought there was something and he wasn't telling me.

139
00:08:03,620 --> 00:08:07,260
Then the pilot said in a conversation that the staff is not available.

140
00:08:07,340 --> 00:08:14,220
Now for the viewers who live in Pakistan or who are not in other countries, Western countries,

141
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:15,950
the airport closes at 11 o'clock in foreign countries.

142
00:08:16,030 --> 00:08:16,950
Right?

143
00:08:17,030 --> 00:08:19,950
It's not locked, but there's no staff.

144
00:08:20,030 --> 00:08:23,950
Because there's a disturbance at night, so all the flights come in the morning.

145
00:08:24,030 --> 00:08:27,950
So if you look at the world map, that's why the Middle East is a hub,

146
00:08:28,030 --> 00:08:33,950
because flights fly from here in the morning, westward, so that they land in the morning, afternoon, or evening.

147
00:08:34,030 --> 00:08:36,950
Recently, a very famous incident happened.

148
00:08:37,030 --> 00:08:42,260
I read on Unilad that a flight was coming to New Zealand, and the airport was also closed at 11 PM.

149
00:08:42,340 --> 00:08:47,260
The flight was 10 minutes late, so the flight had to turn back.

150
00:08:47,340 --> 00:08:51,260
Now I don't know if there is enough fuel or not.

151
00:08:51,340 --> 00:08:56,260
Because the Malaysian airline also had 6 hours of fuel left after leaving Beijing.

152
00:08:56,340 --> 00:08:59,260
So correct me if I'm wrong, but this happens.

153
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:03,260
Heathrow and Vithro all closed because Heathrow is surrounded by houses in the middle of the city.

154
00:09:03,340 --> 00:09:05,260
So the residents complain.

155
00:09:05,340 --> 00:09:09,340
Now the whole night passes from Model Colony, poor people can't sleep.

156
00:09:09,580 --> 00:09:11,240
But here, no one listens to anyone.

157
00:09:11,320 --> 00:09:17,620
So, since the airport was closed, there was no staff to check whether the tires are okay or not, whether it will be able to land next or not.

158
00:09:17,700 --> 00:09:20,880
So, after an hour and a half, they said, the jet bridge is set, you all can get off.

159
00:09:20,960 --> 00:09:25,880
Okay, people were very polite, there was no fight or argument about why we were sitting or what happened.

160
00:09:25,960 --> 00:09:30,420
Everybody understood that it's an emergency, it can happen to anyone, it happened to that person.

161
00:09:30,500 --> 00:09:33,720
So, we got off and then they gave us a voucher, this is the hotel.

162
00:09:33,800 --> 00:09:35,830
The shuttle is outside, you go and sleep in the morning flight.

163
00:09:35,910 --> 00:09:40,790
The flight was at 11 AM and it was delayed to 11 AM.

164
00:09:40,870 --> 00:09:45,110
Since the flight was not from there, they had to arrange extra food.

165
00:09:45,190 --> 00:09:52,070
Now, this is like when you suddenly order food for 400 people on a Pakwan, he will take time, right?

166
00:09:52,150 --> 00:09:55,030
So, since the flight was not from there, it took time to get food.

167
00:09:55,110 --> 00:09:59,030
Then they announced that those who requested for halal food are not available.

168
00:09:59,110 --> 00:10:00,550
We are taking whatever is available as soon as possible.

169
00:10:00,630 --> 00:10:03,100
The flight was delayed from 11 AM to 1 AM, then 2 AM, then 3 AM, and then 4 AM.

170
00:10:03,180 --> 00:10:05,100
Again, no fight.

171
00:10:05,180 --> 00:10:08,100
No fighting. They are very patient.

172
00:10:08,180 --> 00:10:11,100
Anyways, so I left one day earlier.

173
00:10:11,180 --> 00:10:14,100
1 PM. The next day at 4 PM. I am in America.

174
00:10:14,180 --> 00:10:17,100
Then I took a 14 hour flight from Doha.

175
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:21,100
And since the connection from Doha to Karachi, I had gone there one night earlier.

176
00:10:21,180 --> 00:10:24,100
Because I was 24 hours late.

177
00:10:24,180 --> 00:10:27,100
So they said, the next flight is after 12 hours.

178
00:10:27,180 --> 00:10:30,440
So I was like, what is this? I understood. I knew the schedule.

179
00:10:30,520 --> 00:10:34,840
I told him to give me a visa and I'll come to Doha one day.

180
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:38,160
He said that the condition is that you have to book a two-day hotel.

181
00:10:38,240 --> 00:10:44,600
There is a counter in Discover Qatar where you have to book a ticket.

182
00:10:44,680 --> 00:10:50,760
For those people who want to get an on-arrival visa on Pakistani passport,

183
00:10:50,840 --> 00:10:55,680
they don't accept booking.com hotels. They say you have to book from Discover Qatar.

184
00:10:55,760 --> 00:10:57,410
So there is a counter there where you have to book.

185
00:10:57,490 --> 00:11:01,410
So I told him to give me a cheaper one because I don't want to stay for two days.

186
00:11:01,490 --> 00:11:06,410
So I got a $70 hotel which I didn't even see where it is, nor did I read where it is.

187
00:11:06,490 --> 00:11:10,410
My friend was outside, we spent a day. It was 45 degrees.

188
00:11:10,490 --> 00:11:15,410
But there are ACs everywhere. So I had a good day there with my friend Abdul Waheed.

189
00:11:15,490 --> 00:11:19,410
And then I came to Karachi after 3-3.5 days.

190
00:11:19,490 --> 00:11:23,410
So this was the overall trip. World cup was useless, the return trip was weird.

191
00:11:23,490 --> 00:11:25,490
It was very hot in half the places.

192
00:11:25,633 --> 00:11:30,018
The hotel in New York was so small that when the door was opening,

193
00:11:30,098 --> 00:11:32,853
it was sitting and sticking to the floor.

194
00:11:32,933 --> 00:11:37,353
And the washroom was also so that when it was opening, it was completely in sync.

195
00:11:37,433 --> 00:11:39,853
I mean, it was made with such delicacy.

196
00:11:39,933 --> 00:11:42,353
I was too expensive, but this is what it is.

197
00:11:42,433 --> 00:11:43,853
So this was the all-in-all trip.

198
00:11:43,933 --> 00:11:45,853
And I'm sorry I bored you so much.

199
00:11:45,933 --> 00:11:47,353
Let's move on to today's questions.

200
00:11:47,433 --> 00:11:49,353
But before that, don't forget to subscribe.

201
00:11:49,433 --> 00:11:52,433
